cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use meshforge in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "meshforge"
abstract: >-
  An AI copilot takes one routine CT of an abdominal aortic aneurysm from scan
  to physics on a laptop: aorta outline, aneurysm crop, a quality-gated wall
  mesh, wall stress (CalculiX), an investigational strength index and blood
  flow (OpenFOAM), with every reported number taken from the tools.
  Research software: not a medical device, not for diagnosis or treatment.
authors:
  - family-names: "Sirtas"
    given-names: "Levent"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/LeventS2005/meshforge"
url: "https://github.com/LeventS2005/meshforge"
keywords:
  - finite-element-analysis
  - computational-fluid-dynamics
  - hexahedral-meshing
  - abdominal-aortic-aneurysm
  - cardiovascular-biomechanics
  - scientific-computing
